🚽 Test case: poke_int's STDROT_PTR parameter is declared at pointer_level
🚽 0 (a plain rizz*, expected pointer level 1) -- passing a rizz** must be
🚽 rejected statically, not silently truncated/reinterpreted to whatever
🚽 the wrong indirection level happens to point at.
skibidi main {
    rizz value = 10;
    rizz *p = &value;
    rizz **pp = &p;
    poke_int(pp, 5);
    bussin 0;
}
